claim.claim-text:
1. A method comprising:
receiving into a computer processor, preoperative face Input Data for a preoperative face of a patient, said preoperative face Input Data captured by a facial recognition system;
using an artificial intelligence (AI) Engine module to process the preoperative face Input Data;
using the AI Engine module to generate a first procedure plan based on the preoperative face Input Data;
generating a first visualization of a predicted postoperative face of the patient as predicted by the AI Engine module based on the preoperative face Input Data and the first procedure plan generated by the AI Engine module;
storing the first visualization of the predicted postoperative face of the patient;
and displaying the first visualization of the predicted postoperative face of the patient through a Visualization module;
and further comprising
receiving user Input Data entered into an Input module by a user;
using the AI Engine module to process the user Input Data;
using the AI Engine module to generate the first procedure plan based on the user Input Data and the at least one artificial intelligence model;
generating the first visualization of the predicted postoperative face of the patient as predicted by the AI Engine module based on the user Input Data and the first procedure plan generated by the AI Engine module; and
after the first procedure plan is executed on the preoperative face of the patient to form an actual postoperative face of the patient, receiving postoperative feedback at the AI Engine Module;
wherein the postoperative feedback includes grading as to how close the predicted postoperative face of the patient is to the actual postoperative face of the patient; and
and wherein the AI Engine module uses the postoperative feedback to refine the at least one artificial intelligence model.

8. A computing system comprising:
at least one computer processor;
an artificial intelligence (AI) Engine module comprising at least one artificial intelligence model;
a computer memory that stores instructions that, when executed by the at least one computer processor, causes the at least one computer processor to perform operations, including:
receiving Input Data entered into an Input module by a user;
using the AI Engine module to process the Input Data;
using the AI Engine module to generate a first procedure plan based on the Input Data and the at least one artificial intelligence model;
generating a first visualization of a predicted postoperative face of a patient as predicted by the AI Engine module based on the Input Data and the first procedure plan generated by the AI Engine module;
storing the first visualization of the predicted postoperative face of the patient, in a computer memory;
displaying the first visualization of the predicted postoperative face of the patient through a Visualization module; and
after the first procedure plan is executed on a preoperative face of the patient to form an actual postoperative face of the patient, receiving postoperative feedback at the AI Engine Module;
wherein the postoperative feedback includes grading as to how close the predicted postoperative face of the patient is to the actual postoperative face of the patient;
and wherein the AI Engine module uses the postoperative feedback to refine the at least one artificial intelligence model.

9. The computing system of claim 8 wherein:
the computer memory stores instructions that, when executed by the at least one computer processor, causes the at least one computer processor to perform operations, including:
receiving preoperative face Input Data for a preoperative face of the patient, said preoperative face Input Data captured by a facial recognition system;
using the AI Engine module to process the preoperative face Input Data;
using the AI Engine module to generate the first procedure plan based on the preoperative face Input Data;
generating the first visualization of the predicted postoperative face of the patient as predicted by the AI Engine module based on the preoperative Input Data and the first procedure plan generated by the AI Engine module;
storing the first visualization of the predicted postoperative face of the patient, in a computer memory; and
displaying the first visualization of the predicted postoperative face of the patient through a Visualization module.

13. The computing system of claim 12 wherein:
the first procedure plan includes surgical markings;
wherein the at least one computer processor is configured to generate the first visualization of the preoperative face of the patient with surgical markings shown overlaid on top of the preoperative face of the patient by use of the AI Engine module;
wherein modification of the first procedure plan by the user include modification to the surgical markings.

16. The computing system of claim 8 wherein:
the computer memory stores instructions that, when executed by the at least one computer processor, causes the at least one computer processor to perform operations, including:
receiving preoperative face Input Data for a preoperative face of the patient, said preoperative face Input Data captured by a facial recognition system;
using the AI Engine module to process the preoperative face Input Data;
using the AI Engine module to generate the first procedure plan based on the preoperative face Input Data;
generating the first visualization of the predicted postoperative face of the patient as predicted by the AI Engine module based on the preoperative face Input Data and the first procedure plan generated by the AI Engine module;
storing the first visualization of the postoperative face of the patient in a computer memory;
displaying the first visualization of the postoperative face of the patient through the Visualization module; and
physically marking the preoperative face of the patient by use of a marking device to mark the first procedure plan on the patient's face.

17. The computing system of claim 8 wherein:
the computer memory stores instructions that, when executed by the at least one computer processor, causes the at least one computer processor to perform operations, including:
receiving preoperative face Input Data for a preoperative face of a patient, said preoperative face Input Data captured by a facial recognition system;
using the AI Engine module to process the preoperative face Input Data;
using the AI Engine module to generate the first procedure plan based on the preoperative face Input Data;
generating the first visualization of a postoperative face of the patient as predicted by the AI Engine module based on the preoperative face Input Data and the first procedure plan generated by the AI Engine module;
storing the first visualization of the postoperative face of the patient in a computer memory;
displaying the first visualization of the postoperative face of the patient, through the Visualization module; and
wherein the AI Engine module processes the preoperative face Input Data captured by the facial recognition system to determine a set of demographics data for the patient;
and wherein the AI Engine module uses the set of demographics data to generate the first procedure plan.

18. The computing system of claim 8 wherein:
the computer memory stores instructions that, when executed by the at least one computer processor, causes the at least one computer processor to perform operations, including:
receiving preoperative face Input Data for a preoperative face of a patient, said preoperative face Input Data captured by a facial recognition system;
using the AI Engine module to process the preoperative face Input Data;
using the AI Engine module to generate the first procedure plan based on the preoperative face Input Data;
generating the first visualization of a postoperative patient's face as predicted by the AI Engine module based on the preoperative face Input Data and the first procedure plan generated by the AI Engine module;
storing the first visualization of the postoperative face of the patient in a computer memory;
displaying the first visualization of the postoperative patient's face of the patient, through the Visualization module; and
wherein the AI Engine module processes the preoperative face Input Data captured by the facial recognition system to determine medical history for the patient;
and wherein the AI Engine module uses the medical history for the patient to generate the first procedure plan.
